zreader dictionary format 1 (little-endian, all offsets bounds-checked)
32-byte header: magic[8]="ZRWN3001", uint32 keycount,indexoff,keyoff,refoff,glossoff,end.
16-byte sorted-key index records: uint32 keyoffset; uint16 keylength,refcount;
uint32 refoffset,reserved=0. Key offsets relative to keyoff (not NUL terminated).
Reference arrays: uint32 gloss offsets, relative to glossoff; glosses UTF-8/NUL.
References preserve WordNet's frequency-first sense order within each part of speech.
Noun/verb/adjective/adverb senses share gloss storage; multi-word lemmas use spaces.
